                            "neuter"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cb5c6a2-6eb7-4c80-953b-c17fcc5de1b4",
                                "sense_id": "4295f31f-fbe5-3faf-9e77-96ffa611188b",
                                "text": "Weledele Heer,\nDoor ons a.s. vertrek naar Indië, zien wij ons, tot onzen grooten spijt, gedwongen, ons lidmaatschap van de Filmliga, voor het volgend seizoen te beëindigen.",
                                "translation": "Dear Sir,\nDue to our upcoming departure for the Dutch East Indies, we are forced, to our great regret, to end our membership of the Film League for the next season.",
                                "english": "Dear Sir,\nDue to our upcoming departure for the Dutch East Indies, we are forced, to our great regret, to end our membership of the Film League for the next season."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddca607e-0d16-4201-acb9-8138b555a58d",
                                "sense_id": "4295f31f-fbe5-3faf-9e77-96ffa611188b",
                                "text": "En zo blijkt Indië, ondanks ons aanvankelijk voorbehoud, toch in allerlei nuances en op allerlei niveaus haar stempel op zijn werk te hebben gedrukt. Altijd is er, hoe dan ook, die tjap.",
                                "translation": "And so, despite our initial reservations, the Dutch East Indies turn out to have left their impression on his work in all kinds of nuances and at all kinds of levels. There is always, no matter what, that mark.",
                                "english": "And so, despite our initial reservations, the Dutch East Indies turn out to have left their impression on his work in all kinds of nuances and at all kinds of levels. There is always, no matter what, that mark."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39c6e730-5c28-3168-8e48-ad7cf5c7bae1",
                        "entry_id": "3f12e894-c32a-3149-9e0b-3f612e05dc05",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the Indies",
                            "the East Indies",
                            "ellipsis of Nederlands-Indië (“Dutch East Indies”), Indonesia in the context of Dutch colonial rule",
                            "the Indonesian War of Independence"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Indonesia",
                            "Netherlands",
                            "colloquial",
                            "dated",
                            "historical",
                            "informal",
                            "metonymically",
                            "neuter"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8822ff4-474a-4ab6-95c2-76ea4e34fa33",
                                "sense_id": "39c6e730-5c28-3168-8e48-ad7cf5c7bae1",
                                "text": "Voor de zoveelste keer in haar leven opent Anna Weierink het sigarenkistje dat voor haar vader de bijna dagelijkse band was met Indië. Er zitten foto’s in. (...) De beelden zijn onmiskenbaar verbonden met Indië. Groepsfoto’s in het oerwoud of op de boot, begrafenissen, de graven van gestorven kameraden, vrachtwagens op stoffige wegen, landschappen, portretten.",
                                "translation": "For the umpteenth time in her life, Anna Weierink opens the cigar box that was her father's almost daily link to the Dutch East Indies. There are photographs inside (...) The images are unmistakably linked to the Indonesian war of independence. Group photos in the jungle or on the boat, funerals, the graves of dead comrades, trucks on dusty roads, landscapes, portraits.",
                                "english": "For the umpteenth time in her life, Anna Weierink opens the cigar box that was her father's almost daily link to the Dutch East Indies. There are photographs inside (...) The images are unmistakably linked to the Indonesian war of independence. Group photos in the jungle or on the boat, funerals, the graves of dead comrades, trucks on dusty roads, landscapes, portraits."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bf10df5e-abe6-33e7-8c86-82864243ded1",
                        "entry_id": "3f12e894-c32a-3149-9e0b-3f612e05dc05",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the Indies",
                            "the East Indies",
                            "synonym of Indonesië (“Indonesia”); used to refer to the territory and cultural sphere of Indonesia, irrespective of its political status"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Netherlands",
                            "dated",
                            "historical",
                            "informal",
                            "neuter"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a847972-88a9-42c5-8ed2-98efd0e7a8e0",
                                "sense_id": "bf10df5e-abe6-33e7-8c86-82864243ded1",
                                "text": "En weet u, ik heb thuis zo′n groot schilderij hangen. Dat verbeeldt natuurlijk lndië, ja? Adoeh, beeldig. Beeldig!",
                                "translation": "And do you know, I have a big painting hanging at home. Obviously, it depicts Indonesia, right? My goodness, it's gorgeous. Gorgeous!",
                                "english": "And do you know, I have a big painting hanging at home. Obviously, it depicts Indonesia, right? My goodness, it's gorgeous. Gorgeous!"
                            }
                        ]
